      "tarball_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/rodrigojager/pi-subagent/tarball/v0.12.4-rodrigo.1",
      "zipball_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/rodrigojager/pi-subagent/zipball/v0.12.4-rodrigo.1",
      "body": "Delegated work now displays the task and current activity before its metrics. Random adjective/noun nicknames are replaced by numbered runs such as `review #1` and `build #2`.\n\n- Compact live cards show the task without expansion; expanded cards retain its full normalized text.\n- `/jobs` shows tasks, live tool activity, and separate metric/model footers.\n- Completed and stopped cards retain the delegated task. Older records with legacy labels still render.\n- Unicode truncation preserves emoji and terminal column widths.\n\nThis is Rodrigo's UI fork of `mystilleef/pi-subagent` 0.12.4, based on commit `9d5c7501df9812394d2c881f6fc8f503d38b4531`. Original authorship and MIT license are preserved. Child process execution, agent definitions, model selection, nested delegation, cancellation, and result delivery retain the upstream behavior.\n\nValidation: `bun check` on Windows, `bun verify` on Ubuntu (1,837 tests passed), package-content validation (46 files, source hashes matched), and loading both source and packaged extension through the Pi 1.0.0 host loader. Tests cover simulated child processes; no paid model request was needed. The screenshot uses example data rendered by the plugin.\n\nSwitch the configured package:\n\n```sh\npi remove npm:@mystilleef/pi-subagent\npi install https://github.com/rodrigojager/pi-subagent\n```\n\nUse `/reload` in an existing Pi session. Keep one subagent implementation configured. Future updates: `pi update https://github.com/rodrigojager/pi-subagent`.\n\nDistribution is through this GitHub fork and its release assets; the upstream npm package is not republished. SHA-256 checksums are attached.\n"
    }
